speechtext:
That is right under the clause my hon. friend has read. The exempting provision is as follows:
Equipment, at a price in excess of five hundred dollars per unit, specially designed for use directly for road making, road cleaning or fire fighting, but not including automobiles or ordinary motor trucks;
It is quite clear that leaving out ordinary motor trucks and automobiles, the clause provides that equipment that is used directly on road making, road cleaning or fire fighting and which costs more than $500 is exempt.
